e of the examples of North  Macedonia and Albania which have taken  clear steps forward  that strengthens self-confidence in  those countries and makes clear to  others in the region of the western  Balkans but taking the step to join is  worth the  efforts  furthermore we cannot forget that beyond  the question of accession in the  narrower sense progress is made along  the path to membership the Western  Balkans accession process began in  Berlin years ago  I remember that it was very tedious at  first  but when I think about the last Summit I  think that travel with personal identity  cards reciprocal recognition of school  and University diplomas and degrees the  willingness of European support despite  Rising Energy prices  those are significant steps forward  so I understand the impatience no  question but we are not in a phase that  calls for dejectedness certainly not  because of Ukraine as we continue to  keep our eye on the western Balkan  States and on North Macedonia and  Albania where there has been progress  the EU expects fast reforms from the  Western Balkans but also says that it  must perform itself before it can take  in new members and begin negotiations  how long do you think that process will  actually last  it should go as quickly as possible but  I'll admit that at this moment I do not  see signs suggesting the Swift reform of  European institutions  since I have known European institutions  from the inside for years I know that we  have had a series of multiple crises  we remember the Eurozone crisis  we remember more clearly the so-called  Refugee crisis in 2015 and 2016.  we had a huge challenge for the European  Union in fighting the coronavirus  pandemic  naturally these crises all followed one  another in Rapid succession and as we  can see now some like the pandemic and  the Russian invasion of Ukraine continue  to weigh upon us  that absorbs a lot of energy while at  the same time not leaving much mental  capacity for inner reforms which I will  concede are desperately needed  most of the western Balkan states have  shown great solidarity during the war in  Ukraine they have implemented sanctions  against Russia despite major concerns  about the consequences but Serbia has  repeatedly put its close ties to Moscow  on display is the EU doing enough to  support the Western Balkans in their  solidarity with Ukraine and how should  it deal with Serbia  um  to answer the first part of your  question that is one of the reasons I am  visiting the region because of course I  also want to get a feel for the mood in  those countries  and I think we will get a clear picture  of the mood whether North Macedonia and  Albania in this situation in which they  have not only showed solidarity with  Ukraine not only proven themselves by  helping increase economic pressure on  Russia but rather where countries like  North Macedonia and Albania also fulfill  their obligations within NATO and even  beyond that for Albania which currently  sits on the UN Security Council  I'd say that's quite a lot that we can  look at that we should respect  but it should also spark self-confidence  in those countries  I'm sure I will get a sense of whether  that is the case during my trip  to answer the second part of your  question regarding Serbia we have to  continue efforts to convince Serbia that  the path it is currently following is  Raising questions and concerns about how  serious the country is about finding its  way into Europe  um  I've been accompanying the Western  Balkans Journey towards the European  Union for nearly 20 years  and I've been to Serbia often  I'm certain that the people of Serbia  don't want to step away from the desire  shared with many other Western Balkan  states to grow closer to the European  Union and eventually become a member  therefore I can only hope and continue  to attempt to convince Serbia's  political leadership to pursue this path  more clearly  a word about this conflict between  Serbia and Kosovo but has been settled  at the last minute  what can Germany and Europe do to  contain this security risk in the region  in the long term that will have to  answer them and  investing conflicts  as for the conflict I find it A fitting  final question because its resolution  shows once again how important Europe  and the European Union are for the  region  if there were no desire to look to  Europe then Europe would not have  negotiating leverage in such conflicts  between Serbia and Kosovo  nevertheless I am still convinced that  it is the desire to come to Europe to  eventually join the European Union a  wish that is prominent in all of the  western Balkan states that gives Europe  leverage and the possibility to  negotiate and thus the ability to help  find a solution in this seemingly tiny  at least in our eyes seemingly  manageable conflict over automobile  license plates  if tiny conflicts can be dealt with then  perhaps larger conflicts could also be  peacefully resolved contributing to a  normalization of relations between  Serbia and Kosovo  president steinmeier thanks for speaking  to us thank you
 

